1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,960
Level one, zero dollars.

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:06,172
You step off a curb wrong on the way to a shift you can't miss.

3
00:00:06,522 --> 00:00:08,273
Your right wrist bends back.

4
00:00:08,623 --> 00:00:11,001
A small sound, like a knuckle cracking.

5
00:00:11,351 --> 00:00:13,597
By noon it's the size of an orange.

6
00:00:13,947 --> 00:00:16,524
By nine at night you can't hold a fork.

7
00:00:16,874 --> 00:00:17,929
It's a sprain.

8
00:00:18,279 --> 00:00:19,310
Not broken.

9
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:20,813
Just a sprain.

10
00:00:21,163 --> 00:00:24,586
The bill is $4,280.

11
00:00:24,936 --> 00:00:26,177
You don't know that yet.

12
00:00:26,527 --> 00:00:31,622
At the emergency room, a woman at registration turns a tablet toward you.

13
00:00:31,972 --> 00:00:34,237
Financial responsibility form.

14
00:00:34,587 --> 00:00:36,252
You sign with your left hand.

15
00:00:36,602 --> 00:00:39,772
Your name comes out shaky, like a child wrote it.

16
00:00:40,122 --> 00:00:41,883
She doesn't look at the signature.

17
00:00:42,233 --> 00:00:44,537
She looks at the box that says insurance.

18
00:00:44,887 --> 00:00:45,569
Blank.

19
00:00:45,919 --> 00:00:48,225
She taps once and the screen moves on.

20
00:00:48,575 --> 00:00:50,741
You wait three hours and ten minutes.

21
00:00:51,091 --> 00:00:52,109
An X-ray.

22
00:00:52,459 --> 00:00:55,503
A doctor who stays four minutes and never sits down.

23
00:00:55,853 --> 00:01:00,841
A nurse wraps the wrist in a foam splint and hands you a plastic ice bag.

24
00:01:01,191 --> 00:01:03,240
It's cold for maybe twenty minutes.

25
00:01:03,590 --> 00:01:05,582
You leave it on the seat of the bus.

26
00:01:05,932 --> 00:01:07,952
Eighteen days later, it arrives.

27
00:01:08,302 --> 00:01:11,171
A white envelope with a little plastic window.

28
00:01:11,521 --> 00:01:16,106
Your name sits in the window, typed in capitals, like it's been arrested.

29
00:01:16,456 --> 00:01:21,477
Emergency level four, $2,960.

30
00:01:21,827 --> 00:01:25,380
X-ray, two views, $611.

31
00:01:25,730 --> 00:01:28,144
Splint, $412.

32
00:01:28,494 --> 00:01:30,523
Ice bag, $91.

33
00:01:30,873 --> 00:01:32,863
You read that line four times.

34
00:01:33,213 --> 00:01:34,601
Ninety-one dollars.

35
00:01:34,951 --> 00:01:38,401
A bag of frozen peas costs $1.89.

36
00:01:38,751 --> 00:01:41,333
Your mother told you that on the phone that night.

37
00:01:41,683 --> 00:01:42,914
Peas work, she said.

38
00:01:43,264 --> 00:01:44,748
They mold to the joint.

39
00:01:45,098 --> 00:01:50,342
You stick the envelope to the fridge with a magnet from a pizza place that closed.

40
00:01:50,692 --> 00:01:52,050
Then you call the number.

41
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:53,431
Hold music.

42
00:01:53,781 --> 00:01:56,700
A soft piano loop, fourteen seconds long.

43
00:01:57,050 --> 00:02:00,852
It ends on a note that never resolves, then starts again.

44
00:02:01,202 --> 00:02:04,461
You hear it eleven times before a person answers.

45
00:02:04,811 --> 00:02:05,809
She's polite.

46
00:02:06,159 --> 00:02:07,534
She offers a plan.

47
00:02:07,884 --> 00:02:11,572
$180 a month for twenty-four months.

48
00:02:11,922 --> 00:02:14,103
You ask about financial assistance.

49
00:02:14,453 --> 00:02:16,749
She says sure, and lists the documents.

50
00:02:17,099 --> 00:02:18,933
Three months of bank statements.

51
00:02:19,283 --> 00:02:20,748
You get paid on a card.

52
00:02:21,098 --> 00:02:22,339
You don't have a bank.

53
00:02:22,689 --> 00:02:26,291
She says, is there anything else I can help you with today?

54
00:02:26,641 --> 00:02:28,179
Her voice doesn't change.

55
00:02:28,529 --> 00:02:29,987
That's what stays with you.

56
00:02:30,337 --> 00:02:31,430
Not cruelty.

57
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:34,402
Just a script that doesn't have a page for you.

58
00:02:34,752 --> 00:02:37,119
You miss the third payment by two days.

59
00:02:37,469 --> 00:02:39,467
A $35 late fee.

60
00:02:39,817 --> 00:02:43,601
Then a different envelope, from a company you've never heard of.

61
00:02:43,951 --> 00:02:44,804
Collections.

62
00:02:45,154 --> 00:02:46,163
Same window.

63
00:02:46,513 --> 00:02:47,717
Same capitals.

64
00:02:48,067 --> 00:02:51,358
Eight months later, you apply for a cheaper apartment.

65
00:02:51,708 --> 00:02:53,607
The landlord runs your credit.

66
00:02:53,957 --> 00:02:55,246
He looks at the screen.

67
00:02:55,596 --> 00:02:56,553
Then at you.

68
00:02:56,903 --> 00:02:59,317
Then he says the unit just got rented.

69
00:02:59,667 --> 00:03:01,588
Your wrist healed in five weeks.

70
00:03:01,938 --> 00:03:03,725
The bill is still on your record.

71
00:03:04,075 --> 00:03:06,323
The first rule of the hospital bill.

72
00:03:06,673 --> 00:03:08,869
At zero, the bill isn't a request.

73
00:03:09,219 --> 00:03:10,332
It's a sentence.

74
00:03:10,682 --> 00:03:12,054
Paid in installments.

75
00:03:13,254 --> 00:03:15,536
Level two, $5,000.

76
00:03:15,886 --> 00:03:17,389
You have insurance now.

77
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:18,920
The cheap plan.

78
00:03:19,270 --> 00:03:21,945
A $7,500 deductible.

79
00:03:22,295 --> 00:03:27,357
Which means the card in your wallet is mostly a promise about other people's money.

80
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:29,925
A kidney stone wakes you at 4 a.m.

81
00:03:30,275 --> 00:03:33,966
Pain so complete you can't remember being anything else.

82
00:03:34,316 --> 00:03:35,538
A CT scan.

83
00:03:35,888 --> 00:03:36,740
Fluids.

84
00:03:37,090 --> 00:03:39,155
A prescription you fill and ration.

85
00:03:39,505 --> 00:03:41,540
You've already learned to fear the door.

86
00:03:41,890 --> 00:03:44,272
Last month your throat burned for a week.

87
00:03:44,622 --> 00:03:47,350
You called urgent care to ask the price first.

88
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:51,045
The woman said she couldn't tell you until after the visit.

89
00:03:51,395 --> 00:03:55,393
So you gargled salt water for nine days and called it a choice.

90
00:03:55,743 --> 00:03:57,666
This time, two envelopes come.

91
00:03:58,016 --> 00:04:01,581
The first says, in bold across the top, THIS IS NOT A BILL.

92
00:04:01,931 --> 00:04:05,763
It shows the hospital charged $8,900.

93
00:04:06,113 --> 00:04:11,752
Your insurer negotiated it down to $3,140.

94
00:04:12,102 --> 00:04:15,092
A column of numbers people agreed on without you.

95
00:04:15,442 --> 00:04:18,111
And at the bottom, the amount the plan paid.

96
00:04:18,461 --> 00:04:19,182
Zero.

97
00:04:19,532 --> 00:04:21,480
The second envelope is the bill.

98
00:04:21,830 --> 00:04:24,784
$3,140.

99
00:04:25,134 --> 00:04:26,091
All yours.

100
00:04:26,441 --> 00:04:28,443
You never get close to the deductible.

101
00:04:28,793 --> 00:04:30,518
Nobody on this plan does.

102
00:04:30,868 --> 00:04:32,785
The stone was four millimeters.

103
00:04:33,135 --> 00:04:35,037
The bill is a month of rent.

104
00:04:35,387 --> 00:04:36,694
You scan the lines.

105
00:04:37,044 --> 00:04:37,999
There it is.

106
00:04:38,349 --> 00:04:40,379
Ice bag, $91.

107
00:04:40,729 --> 00:04:42,627
You don't remember an ice bag.

108
00:04:42,977 --> 00:04:45,686
You were curled on a gurney with your eyes closed.

109
00:04:46,036 --> 00:04:47,973
Maybe they put one on your back.

110
00:04:48,323 --> 00:04:49,568
Maybe they didn't.

111
00:04:49,918 --> 00:04:51,291
You call the insurer.

112
00:04:51,641 --> 00:04:53,475
Fourteen seconds of piano.

113
00:04:53,825 --> 00:04:55,120
You can hum it now.

114
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:57,319
You know exactly where it loops.

115
00:04:57,669 --> 00:04:58,817
A man answers.

116
00:04:59,167 --> 00:05:00,117
You explain.

117
00:05:00,467 --> 00:05:03,012
He says, I understand your frustration.

118
00:05:03,362 --> 00:05:04,629
You explain again.

119
00:05:04,979 --> 00:05:11,546
He says it again, the same four words, the same pitch, like a key turning in a lock that doesn't open.

120
00:05:11,896 --> 00:05:14,902
At $5,000, you're not uninsured.

121
00:05:15,252 --> 00:05:16,483
You're underinsured.

122
00:05:16,833 --> 00:05:19,603
The only difference is the second envelope.

123
00:05:20,803 --> 00:05:23,200
Level three, $40,000.

124
00:05:23,550 --> 00:05:24,709
A real job.

125
00:05:25,059 --> 00:05:26,215
A real plan.

126
00:05:26,565 --> 00:05:31,044
A $500 deductible and a ceiling you can actually see.

127
00:05:31,394 --> 00:05:35,038
You break your ankle playing pickup basketball on a Saturday.

128
00:05:35,388 --> 00:05:36,544
Surgery Monday.

129
00:05:36,894 --> 00:05:38,442
Two screws and a plate.

130
00:05:38,792 --> 00:05:40,408
You're scared of the surgery.

131
00:05:40,758 --> 00:05:43,630
Then you realize you're more scared of the envelope.

132
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:44,826
It comes.

133
00:05:45,176 --> 00:05:46,404
Same white paper.

134
00:05:46,754 --> 00:05:47,958
Same little window.

135
00:05:48,308 --> 00:05:50,514
But the math inside is different now.

136
00:05:50,864 --> 00:05:54,706
Total charges, $31,200.

137
00:05:55,056 --> 00:05:58,120
Plan paid, $30,060.

138
00:05:58,470 --> 00:06:01,217
You owe, $1,140.

139
00:06:01,567 --> 00:06:03,145
You stare at the middle number.

140
00:06:03,495 --> 00:06:06,372
Thirty thousand dollars somebody else handled.

141
00:06:06,722 --> 00:06:09,705
At level one, you'd have carried that for a decade.

142
00:06:10,055 --> 00:06:11,490
Here it's just a row.

143
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:13,099
Then a surprise.

144
00:06:13,449 --> 00:06:16,856
A separate bill from an anesthesia group you never met.

145
00:06:17,206 --> 00:06:19,063
$2,400.

146
00:06:19,413 --> 00:06:21,162
Your stomach drops out of habit.

147
00:06:21,512 --> 00:06:23,193
But you've learned the words now.

148
00:06:23,543 --> 00:06:26,578
You read them off a website and say them on the phone.

149
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:28,071
The rep pauses.

150
00:06:28,421 --> 00:06:29,648
Puts you on hold.

151
00:06:29,998 --> 00:06:31,565
Six minutes of piano.

152
00:06:31,915 --> 00:06:34,344
It sounds shorter when you know how it ends.

153
00:06:34,694 --> 00:06:35,745
She comes back.

154
00:06:36,095 --> 00:06:37,845
The bill has been withdrawn.

155
00:06:38,195 --> 00:06:39,733
Sorry for the confusion.

156
00:06:40,083 --> 00:06:42,736
Nobody taught you that sentence at level one.

157
00:06:43,086 --> 00:06:44,071
That's the thing.

158
00:06:44,421 --> 00:06:46,663
The words existed the whole time.

159
00:06:47,013 --> 00:06:50,041
They just cost $40,000 a year to learn.

160
00:06:50,391 --> 00:06:55,275
Your manager approves two weeks of paid leave without looking up from her screen.

161
00:06:55,625 --> 00:06:59,569
At level one, two weeks off would have cost more than the surgery.

162
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:02,307
You put the envelope on the fridge anyway.

163
00:07:02,657 --> 00:07:03,714
Same magnet.

164
00:07:04,064 --> 00:07:05,187
Old instinct.

165
00:07:05,537 --> 00:07:08,996
At $40,000, the bill stops being a threat.

166
00:07:09,346 --> 00:07:10,762
It becomes paperwork.

167
00:07:11,962 --> 00:07:15,286
Level four, $250,000.

168
00:07:15,636 --> 00:07:17,276
The envelope disappears.

169
00:07:17,626 --> 00:07:19,547
The bill comes as an email now.

170
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:21,422
Your statement is ready.

171
00:07:21,772 --> 00:07:26,035
You open the patient portal and pay with your face in four seconds.

172
00:07:26,385 --> 00:07:27,786
You don't read the lines.

173
00:07:28,136 --> 00:07:30,347
You just watch the balance turn green.

174
00:07:30,697 --> 00:07:33,395
You need an MRI for your lower back.

175
00:07:33,745 --> 00:07:37,883
You find out the hospital charges $3,200.

176
00:07:38,233 --> 00:07:43,458
An imaging center across town does it for $450 cash.

177
00:07:43,808 --> 00:07:44,875
You pay cash.

178
00:07:45,225 --> 00:07:46,899
It's faster than arguing.

179
00:07:47,249 --> 00:07:49,743
The receptionist asks, card on file?

180
00:07:50,093 --> 00:07:51,623
You have a card on file.

181
00:07:51,973 --> 00:07:55,563
You didn't know you'd become a person with a card on file.

182
00:07:55,913 --> 00:08:00,242
Later, out of curiosity, you open an old visit in the portal.

183
00:08:00,592 --> 00:08:01,540
Itemized.

184
00:08:01,890 --> 00:08:03,920
Ice bag, $91.

185
00:08:04,270 --> 00:08:06,151
You laugh out loud in your kitchen.

186
00:08:06,501 --> 00:08:08,040
Then you close the tab.

187
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:09,496
You don't dispute it.

188
00:08:09,846 --> 00:08:13,940
Ninety-one dollars isn't worth fourteen seconds of piano.

189
00:08:14,290 --> 00:08:15,623
That's when you notice it.

190
00:08:15,973 --> 00:08:17,426
The number didn't change.

191
00:08:17,776 --> 00:08:18,562
You did.

192
00:08:18,912 --> 00:08:20,503
Your mother calls that week.

193
00:08:20,853 --> 00:08:25,418
She's on the phone with the hospital about a fall she took in the parking lot.

194
00:08:25,768 --> 00:08:27,885
She's been on hold for forty minutes.

195
00:08:28,235 --> 00:08:30,404
You tell her to give you the account number.

196
00:08:30,754 --> 00:08:31,585
You call.

197
00:08:31,935 --> 00:08:33,026
The loop starts.

198
00:08:33,376 --> 00:08:35,305
A woman picks up, tired, flat.

199
00:08:35,655 --> 00:08:38,109
You say, I'd like to pay the full balance.

200
00:08:38,459 --> 00:08:40,303
Her voice lifts half an octave.

201
00:08:40,653 --> 00:08:41,527
Of course.

202
00:08:41,877 --> 00:08:42,854
Absolutely.

203
00:08:43,204 --> 00:08:44,704
Let me pull that up for you.

204
00:08:45,054 --> 00:08:46,786
Thirty seconds, and it's gone.

205
00:08:47,136 --> 00:08:50,097
$2,870.

206
00:08:50,447 --> 00:08:53,402
Your mother sends you a photo of the paid statement.

207
00:08:53,752 --> 00:08:55,310
She stuck it to her fridge.

208
00:08:55,660 --> 00:09:00,957
At $250,000, a hospital bill is a notification.

209
00:09:01,307 --> 00:09:03,281
You swipe it away like the weather.

210
00:09:04,481 --> 00:09:06,634
Level five, $2 million.

211
00:09:06,984 --> 00:09:08,583
You stop paying for care.

212
00:09:08,933 --> 00:09:10,224
You pay for access.

213
00:09:10,574 --> 00:09:12,108
A concierge practice.

214
00:09:12,458 --> 00:09:14,453
$15,000 a year.

215
00:09:14,803 --> 00:09:18,638
Your doctor has three hundred patients and one of them is you.

216
00:09:18,988 --> 00:09:21,625
The invoice arrives once, in January.

217
00:09:21,975 --> 00:09:22,842
One line.

218
00:09:23,192 --> 00:09:24,417
Annual membership.

219
00:09:24,767 --> 00:09:25,788
No codes.

220
00:09:26,138 --> 00:09:27,432
No ice bags.

221
00:09:27,782 --> 00:09:28,879
It's 2 a.m.

222
00:09:29,229 --> 00:09:30,754
and your chest feels tight.

223
00:09:31,104 --> 00:09:32,007
You text.

224
00:09:32,357 --> 00:09:34,143
She answers in four minutes.

225
00:09:34,493 --> 00:09:36,034
She asks three questions.

226
00:09:36,384 --> 00:09:37,471
It's anxiety.

227
00:09:37,821 --> 00:09:41,707
She tells you to breathe, and stays on the phone until you do.

228
00:09:42,057 --> 00:09:43,781
There's no bill for that call.

229
00:09:44,131 --> 00:09:45,477
It's already been paid.

230
00:09:45,827 --> 00:09:46,892
Months ago.

231
00:09:47,242 --> 00:09:48,742
Before anything hurt.

232
00:09:49,092 --> 00:09:51,752
In March she makes a house call for a fever.

233
00:09:52,102 --> 00:09:55,032
She sits on the arm of your couch for fifty minutes.

234
00:09:55,382 --> 00:09:59,421
At level one, a doctor stayed four minutes and never sat down.

235
00:09:59,771 --> 00:10:00,805
Same degree.

236
00:10:01,155 --> 00:10:02,208
Same training.

237
00:10:02,558 --> 00:10:06,775
The only thing that changed is which side of the retainer you're on.

238
00:10:07,125 --> 00:10:09,754
When you do need a hospital, she calls ahead.

239
00:10:10,104 --> 00:10:11,800
A form appears pre-filled.

240
00:10:12,150 --> 00:10:14,350
Nobody turns a tablet toward you.

241
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:17,321
Nobody watches the insurance box.

242
00:10:17,671 --> 00:10:19,744
Her assistant emails afterward.

243
00:10:20,094 --> 00:10:23,849
Would you like us to send the statement directly to your accountant?

244
00:10:24,199 --> 00:10:27,757
It's the first time anyone has assumed you have an accountant.

245
00:10:28,107 --> 00:10:29,146
You say yes.

246
00:10:29,496 --> 00:10:31,210
You don't see the itemization.

247
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:33,946
You'll never know if there was an ice bag.

248
00:10:34,296 --> 00:10:35,606
You realize something.

249
00:10:35,956 --> 00:10:38,698
At level one, you were billed for every minute.

250
00:10:39,048 --> 00:10:41,663
Now you're billed for minutes that never happen.

251
00:10:42,013 --> 00:10:43,675
The calm is the product.

252
00:10:44,025 --> 00:10:47,087
At $2 million, you don't pay for treatment.

253
00:10:47,437 --> 00:10:48,965
You pay for the phone number.

254
00:10:50,165 --> 00:10:52,839
Level six, $25 million.

255
00:10:53,189 --> 00:10:55,112
The bill doesn't come to you at all.

256
00:10:55,462 --> 00:10:56,784
Your knee wears out.

257
00:10:57,134 --> 00:11:00,461
Old ankle, bad landing, a body that kept score.

258
00:11:00,811 --> 00:11:05,300
You have it replaced at a private surgical hospital two states away.

259
00:11:05,650 --> 00:11:06,467
A plane.

260
00:11:06,817 --> 00:11:08,886
A car at the bottom of the stairs.

261
00:11:09,236 --> 00:11:12,243
A suite with a nurse who knocks before she enters.

262
00:11:12,593 --> 00:11:13,753
You sign nothing.

263
00:11:14,103 --> 00:11:19,973
Someone signed for you weeks ago, in a steady hand, with your full name spelled correctly.

264
00:11:20,323 --> 00:11:24,112
At level one, you signed with your left hand, and nobody looked.

265
00:11:24,462 --> 00:11:28,063
The price is $142,000.

266
00:11:28,413 --> 00:11:35,521
You know that only because it shows up three weeks later as a single row in your family office's monthly report.

267
00:11:35,871 --> 00:11:36,626
Medical.

268
00:11:36,976 --> 00:11:40,606
$142,300.

269
00:11:40,956 --> 00:11:43,342
Between landscaping and a wine order.

270
00:11:43,692 --> 00:11:44,877
That's the bill now.

271
00:11:45,227 --> 00:11:47,309
A line in someone else's spreadsheet.

272
00:11:47,659 --> 00:11:48,665
You don't hold it.

273
00:11:49,015 --> 00:11:50,124
You don't open it.

274
00:11:50,474 --> 00:11:53,782
A person you pay is paid to make sure you never have to.

275
00:11:54,132 --> 00:11:59,033
On discharge day, the director of patient experience walks you to the car.

276
00:11:59,383 --> 00:12:00,306
She's warm.

277
00:12:00,656 --> 00:12:02,557
She asks about your recovery.

278
00:12:02,907 --> 00:12:07,975
Then, lightly, as the door opens, she mentions the hospital foundation.

279
00:12:08,325 --> 00:12:10,356
A new rehabilitation center.

280
00:12:10,706 --> 00:12:12,170
Naming opportunities.

281
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,907
She hands you a card.

282
00:12:14,257 --> 00:12:15,324
Heavy stock.

283
00:12:15,674 --> 00:12:16,518
Embossed.

284
00:12:16,868 --> 00:12:18,831
Not an envelope with a window.

285
00:12:19,181 --> 00:12:20,359
An invitation.

286
00:12:20,709 --> 00:12:24,647
At $25 million, the hospital stops billing you.

287
00:12:24,997 --> 00:12:26,353
It starts courting you.

288
00:12:27,553 --> 00:12:30,305
Level seven, $200 million.

289
00:12:30,655 --> 00:12:33,825
You pay hospital bills for four thousand people.

290
00:12:34,175 --> 00:12:36,107
Your company is self-insured.

291
00:12:36,457 --> 00:12:45,829
Every employee's emergency room, every child's ear infection, every stone and sprain, flows back to a spreadsheet you approve.

292
00:12:46,179 --> 00:12:49,224
Last year, $61 million in claims.

293
00:12:49,574 --> 00:12:51,511
Your CFO walks you through it.

294
00:12:51,861 --> 00:12:53,491
She stops on one slide.

295
00:12:53,841 --> 00:12:55,236
Ancillary supplies.

296
00:12:55,586 --> 00:12:56,747
A single item.

297
00:12:57,097 --> 00:13:00,381
3,112 ice bags.

298
00:13:00,731 --> 00:13:02,558
At $91 each.

299
00:13:02,908 --> 00:13:04,833
Then she proposes a change.

300
00:13:05,183 --> 00:13:08,792
Raise the employee deductible to $6,000.

301
00:13:09,142 --> 00:13:11,849
Saves $4.1 million a year.

302
00:13:12,199 --> 00:13:12,905
Clean.

303
00:13:13,255 --> 00:13:14,192
Defensible.

304
00:13:14,542 --> 00:13:15,743
Industry standard.

305
00:13:16,093 --> 00:13:19,616
You think about yourself, curled on a gurney at 4 a.m.

306
00:13:19,966 --> 00:13:21,054
Two envelopes.

307
00:13:21,404 --> 00:13:23,652
A month of rent for four millimeters.

308
00:13:24,002 --> 00:13:24,975
You say no.

309
00:13:25,325 --> 00:13:27,699
She nods and moves to the next slide.

310
00:13:28,049 --> 00:13:29,376
She doesn't ask why.

311
00:13:29,726 --> 00:13:30,884
You don't explain.

312
00:13:31,234 --> 00:13:33,611
That spring, your mother mentions a lump.

313
00:13:33,961 --> 00:13:34,753
Casually.

314
00:13:35,103 --> 00:13:35,991
Over dinner.

315
00:13:36,341 --> 00:13:38,072
You ask how long it's been there.

316
00:13:38,422 --> 00:13:39,547
She says a while.

317
00:13:39,897 --> 00:13:41,094
You ask how long.

318
00:13:41,444 --> 00:13:43,257
She says since before Christmas.

319
00:13:43,607 --> 00:13:44,497
It's April.

320
00:13:44,847 --> 00:13:46,517
You could have flown her anywhere.

321
00:13:46,867 --> 00:13:47,831
Any surgeon.

322
00:13:48,181 --> 00:13:49,060
Any city.

323
00:13:49,410 --> 00:13:50,253
That night.

324
00:13:50,603 --> 00:13:51,617
She knows that.

325
00:13:51,967 --> 00:13:53,306
She waited anyway.

326
00:13:53,656 --> 00:13:56,013
She said she didn't want to cost you anything.

327
00:13:56,363 --> 00:14:00,257
The best oncologist in the country sees her in two days.

328
00:14:00,607 --> 00:14:02,784
Everything moves at the speed of money.

329
00:14:03,134 --> 00:14:04,597
But it can't move backward.

330
00:14:04,947 --> 00:14:06,473
It can't reach December.

331
00:14:06,823 --> 00:14:08,521
Here's what nobody tells you.

332
00:14:08,871 --> 00:14:12,027
You can pay off every bill your mother will ever get.

333
00:14:12,377 --> 00:14:13,878
You can't pay off the habit.

334
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:17,008
The math she learned at level one never left.

335
00:14:17,358 --> 00:14:19,635
It just waited in her for forty years.

336
00:14:19,985 --> 00:14:21,543
She dies in October.

337
00:14:21,893 --> 00:14:24,555
In her kitchen drawer, you find envelopes.

338
00:14:24,905 --> 00:14:25,736
Dozens.

339
00:14:26,086 --> 00:14:27,706
White, with little windows.

340
00:14:28,056 --> 00:14:29,556
Every one stamped paid.

341
00:14:29,906 --> 00:14:31,299
Every one paid by you.

342
00:14:31,649 --> 00:14:32,763
She kept them all.

343
00:14:33,113 --> 00:14:36,857
At $200 million, you can buy anyone's care.

344
00:14:37,207 --> 00:14:40,514
You can't buy back the time they spent afraid of the price.

345
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:43,951
Level eight, $1 billion.

346
00:14:44,301 --> 00:14:46,285
You don't receive hospital bills.

347
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:48,573
Hospitals send you proposals.

348
00:14:48,923 --> 00:14:51,220
Your own care is no longer billed.

349
00:14:51,570 --> 00:14:53,178
Your doctor is employed.

350
00:14:53,528 --> 00:14:56,154
Salary, benefits, an office in your house.

351
00:14:56,504 --> 00:15:03,860
When your wrist aches in the cold, the old sprain, she's there in nine minutes with an ice pack from your own freezer.

352
00:15:04,210 --> 00:15:13,892
That fall, at a gala, the chief executive of the hospital where you once waited three hours and ten minutes shakes your hand with both of his.

353
00:15:14,242 --> 00:15:17,278
He knows your net worth to the nearest hundred million.

354
00:15:17,628 --> 00:15:19,102
He doesn't know your wrist.

355
00:15:19,452 --> 00:15:21,829
He tells you his door is always open.

356
00:15:22,179 --> 00:15:26,593
You remember a tablet turned toward you, and a box marked insurance.

357
00:15:26,943 --> 00:15:31,222
A founder pitches you on a company that speeds up hospital billing.

358
00:15:31,572 --> 00:15:32,572
Better coding.

359
00:15:32,922 --> 00:15:34,229
Faster collections.

360
00:15:34,579 --> 00:15:35,782
Fewer write-offs.

361
00:15:36,132 --> 00:15:37,039
He's sharp.

362
00:15:37,389 --> 00:15:39,541
He laughs at your jokes a beat early.

363
00:15:39,891 --> 00:15:42,483
He plays a demo of their patient phone line.

364
00:15:42,833 --> 00:15:44,132
The piano starts.

365
00:15:44,482 --> 00:15:45,743
Fourteen seconds.

366
00:15:46,093 --> 00:15:47,914
The note that never resolves.

367
00:15:48,264 --> 00:15:50,263
You haven't heard it in twenty years.

368
00:15:50,613 --> 00:15:52,150
Your hand goes cold.

369
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:54,349
You know exactly where it loops.

370
00:15:54,699 --> 00:15:56,041
You pass on the deal.

371
00:15:56,391 --> 00:15:57,706
You don't tell him why.

372
00:15:58,056 --> 00:15:59,906
Instead, you do something else.

373
00:16:00,256 --> 00:16:03,116
Medical debt sells for about a penny on the dollar.

374
00:16:03,466 --> 00:16:07,985
You buy $40 million of it for $400,000.

375
00:16:08,335 --> 00:16:10,313
Less than the painting in your hallway.

376
00:16:10,663 --> 00:16:12,198
Then you forgive all of it.

377
00:16:12,548 --> 00:16:13,683
Letters go out.

378
00:16:14,033 --> 00:16:15,252
Thousands of them.

379
00:16:15,602 --> 00:16:18,320
White envelopes with little plastic windows.

380
00:16:18,670 --> 00:16:20,701
A name in capitals in every one.

381
00:16:21,051 --> 00:16:22,402
Inside, one line.

382
00:16:22,752 --> 00:16:23,894
Balance, zero.

383
00:16:24,244 --> 00:16:27,315
It changes everything for the people who open them.

384
00:16:27,665 --> 00:16:32,092
It changes nothing about the envelopes that will be printed next month.

385
00:16:32,442 --> 00:16:33,338
You know that.

386
00:16:33,688 --> 00:16:34,977
You do it anyway.

387
00:16:35,327 --> 00:16:38,924
At $1 billion, you don't pay hospital bills.

388
00:16:39,274 --> 00:16:41,555
You decide which ones stop existing.

389
00:16:42,755 --> 00:16:49,388
Somewhere right now, someone is standing in a kitchen holding a white envelope with a little plastic window.

390
00:16:49,738 --> 00:16:52,195
Their name sits inside it in capitals.

391
00:16:52,545 --> 00:16:54,769
Their wrist is wrapped in a foam splint.

392
00:16:55,119 --> 00:16:56,593
It isn't even broken.

393
00:16:56,943 --> 00:16:58,945
They read one line four times.

394
00:16:59,295 --> 00:17:01,325
Ice bag, ninety-one dollars.

395
00:17:01,675 --> 00:17:04,925
A bag of frozen peas is $1.89.

396
00:17:05,275 --> 00:17:09,217
They stick it to the fridge with a magnet from a place that closed.

397
00:17:09,567 --> 00:17:10,763
They call the number.

398
00:17:11,113 --> 00:17:12,947
Fourteen seconds of piano.

399
00:17:13,297 --> 00:17:15,248
They'll hear it eleven times.

400
00:17:15,598 --> 00:17:17,608
Nobody in that building is cruel.

401
00:17:17,958 --> 00:17:20,670
The coder, the clerk, the man with the script.

402
00:17:21,020 --> 00:17:22,950
Everyone is doing their job.

403
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:25,278
And the job is the envelope.

404
00:17:25,628 --> 00:17:28,929
The doctor's hands are nearly the same at every level.

405
00:17:29,279 --> 00:17:31,297
The X-ray is the same X-ray.

406
00:17:31,647 --> 00:17:33,976
The ice bag is the same ice bag.

407
00:17:34,326 --> 00:17:35,974
The bill is what changes.

408
00:17:36,324 --> 00:17:38,347
And the bill decides who you become.

409
00:17:38,697 --> 00:17:39,682
Balance due.

